    "kv_type": "f32",
    "reference_compute_dtype": "f32",
    "_why": "The oracle runs BF16 storage upcast to F32 compute, so the gate pairs it with an F32 GGUF built from the same weights (BF16 -> F32 is lossless; the two files hold identical values). ggml's BF16 kernel rounds activations to BF16 (vec_dot_type=GGML_TYPE_BF16), which torch at F32 does not, so gating the shipped BF16 GGUF here would measure a precision gap ~1000x larger than the graph drift this file is meant to catch. Measured on enc.block.6.out: F32/F32 1.66e-02, F32/BF16 12.76, BF16/BF16 71.13. The shipped BF16 artifact is gated on WER at Stage 4 Step 11 instead."
